{"type":"FeatureCollection","locode":"NZTRG","quays":[],"attribution":"© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0. https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright","position_outside":"UN/LOCODE places Tauranga at (-37.6833, 176.1667), in the city south of Sulphur Point, about 2 km from the container terminal. A ship there would be in the inner harbour or ashore.","position_on_water":false,"selection_digest":"98323bbc5a9395b23eabed5e3640c4b8431dd2ff69f8539788ce9d5cbe84453e","features":[
{"type":"Feature","properties":{"kind":"port_limits","cargo":[],"osm":["relation/13494449","way/77594023"],"source":"Derived: the convex hull of this port's terminals from OpenStreetMap, grown by 300 m, then cut to the water OpenStreetMap maps inside it (the sea within its coastline, rivers, docks and basins), with the terminals kept whole","licence":"ODbL-1.0","reviewed_at":"2026-11-23","clip":"water","note":"OpenStreetMap maps no port limits for Tauranga. These are the hull of the two sides of the port grown by 300 m, cut to the water OpenStreetMap maps inside it, with the terminals kept whole and a 30 m margin where they meet the water. What is left is the Mount Maunganui wharves, the Sulphur Point container terminal and Stella Passage between them; the town of Mount Maunganui between the wharves is cut away. A scan of OpenStreetMap finds no schools, hospitals or places of worship inside. Six houses stand inside the Mount Maunganui wharves' own outline and two more in the margin beside it, eight wholly inside in all, with the edge of a small residential area; the named places are the Sulphur Point label on the container terminal, and the boundaries of Mount Maunganui and its industrial quarter overlap the wharves.","inside":{"houses":8,"residential_m2":93,"residential":[{"osm":"way/77594760","m2":93}],"amenities":0,"places":[{"name":"Sulphur Point","place":"quarter","osm":"node/3939284015"}]}},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[176.167636,-37.66846],[176.167645,-37.66847],[176.167647,-37.66847],[176.167674,-37.669097],[176.16767,-37.669269],[176.167392,-37.670742],[176.167312,-37.671149],[176.167245,-37.671437],[176.167273,-37.671449],[176.167317,-37.671485],[176.167313,-37.671505],[176.167401,-37.671564],[176.167408,-37.6716],[176.167536,-37.671674],[176.167872,-37.671788],[176.168048,-37.671832],[176.168351,-37.671871],[176.169686,-37.671801],[176.169692,-37.671793],[176.1696,-37.670136],[176.169566,-37.670038],[176.169695,-37.670024],[176.169753,-37